# Copy to .env and fill in. Values are examples/placeholders only — never
# commit real credentials. This file documents the variables the app reads so
# a new deployment doesn't silently ship without them.
#
# Only the integrations that fail *silently* are listed exhaustively; add
# others here as they're introduced.

# ─── GoHighLevel (LeadConnector) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by lib/ghl.ts to upsert Early Access signups into GHL Contacts.
# If either of these is missing the signup still succeeds for the user, but the
# contact never reaches GoHighLevel — the failure is only visible in the server
# log ("[ghl] NOT CONFIGURED") and in the signup row's ghl_sync_error column.
#
# GHL_API_KEY     Private Integration Token for the sub-account, with the
#                 contacts.write scope (and contacts.readonly for the admin
#                 retry tooling). Starts with "pit-".
# GHL_LOCATION_ID The GHL location (sub-account) id contacts are upserted into.
GHL_API_KEY=pit-xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx
GHL_LOCATION_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# ─── Cron endpoints ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared secret for the handlers under app/api/cron/*. They compare it against
# `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>` and fail closed (401) when it is unset,
# so an unauthenticated caller can't burn provider quota.
#
# NOT REQUIRED TODAY: no cron is scheduled. The Vercel Cron entry for
# /api/cron/post-detection was removed from vercel.json because the Hobby plan
# permits only one cron run per day and rejects a five-minute schedule at deploy
# time. Set this when the project moves to Pro and the schedule is restored —
# see the header of app/api/cron/post-detection/route.ts.
CRON_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string


# ─── Microsoft / Outlook OAuth (Azure App Registration) ──────────────────────
# Used by app/api/outlook/* (connect → callback → send/threads) for Microsoft
# Graph mail access, via lib/microsoft-oauth.ts.
#
# If MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID is unset the connect route now refuses to build an
# authorize URL and redirects to /dashboard/inbox?outlookError=outlook_not_configured,
# logging "[outlook] connect: Microsoft OAuth is not configured". Before this
# guard existed it silently sent users to Microsoft with client_id=undefined.
#
# Azure portal → App registrations → your app:
#   MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID     Overview → "Application (client) ID" (a GUID).
#   MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET Certificates & secrets → Client secrets → Value.
#                           Server-side only — never expose to the browser.
#
# Register this exact Redirect URI (Web platform) for each origin you deploy to:
#   production  https://instroom.io/api/outlook/callback
#   staging     https://staging-instroom.vercel.app/api/outlook/callback
#   local dev   http://localhost:3000/api/outlook/callback
# The redirect_uri is derived from this deployment's public origin
# (NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL / APP_URL / NEXTAUTH_URL — see lib/app-url.ts), so that
# origin must match the registered URI exactly.
#
# On Vercel, set that origin per environment — the staging deployment must have
#   NEXTAUTH_URL=https://staging-instroom.vercel.app
# or it inherits production's value and Microsoft rejects the exchange with
# redirect_uri_mismatch. /api/outlook/connect logs the exact redirect_uri it
# built and which variable it came from, so a mismatch is visible in the
# deployment's own logs rather than guessed at.
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# ── Instroom influencer API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Host for influencer profile lookups (Influencer List auto-fetch and Influencer
# Discovery). Documented endpoints, appended to this base:
#   Instagram  GET {base}/v2/{username}/instagram
#   TikTok     GET {base}/{username}/tiktok
#   Discovery  GET {base}/users/{query}, /similar/{username},
#                  /hashtags/{query}, /locations/{query}
#
# BOTH variables are needed and they are not interchangeable:
#   INSTROOM_API_BASE_URL             server-side only.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_INSTROOM_API_BASE_URL reaches the browser. The lookup runs
#                                     client-side, so THIS is the one the
#                                     Influencer List actually uses. Next.js
#                                     only inlines NEXT_PUBLIC_-prefixed vars
#                                     into the client bundle.
#
# Set both to the public URL of the deployed API service (Railway → the API
# service → Settings → Networking → Public Domain). No trailing slash needed;
# one is trimmed if present. A host that does not resolve surfaces in the UI as
# "the API could not be reached", with Retry and manual-add — it is never
# reported as "influencer not found".
INSTROOM_API_BASE_URL=https://apiinstroom-production.up.railway.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_INSTROOM_API_BASE_URL=https://apiinstroom-production.up.railway.app
